{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וישלך מידו", :translit "vayishlech miyado", :gloss "and he cast from his hand"} {:he "חסר יו\"ד", :translit "chaser yud", :gloss "defective [missing] yud"} {:he "שכפרו בי' דברות", :translit "shekofru ba'asirit dibrot", :gloss "for they denied the Ten Commandments"} {:he "וי\"פ פסל בתורה", :translit "v'kamu pisul batorah", :gloss "and it appears [as] defective in the Torah"} {:he "וי\"פ תועבת ה' במשלי", :translit "v'kamu to'avat Hashem bamishlei", :gloss "and it appears, 'the abomination of YHWH,' in Proverbs"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "The word מידו is written without a second yud (defective spelling), signaling that Israel broke the covenant by denying the Ten Commandments through the golden calf."} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וישלך מידו" "תועבת ה'"]}], :frame {:text "Moses shatters the tablets upon seeing the golden calf (Exodus 32:19). The midrashic tradition holds that the letters departed from the tablets when Israel sinned with the calf, so that the tablets became too heavy for Moses to carry and he cast them from his hands (Shabbat 87a; Pesikta Rabbati 23). The Ba'al HaTurim links the defective spelling of מידו to the numerical value of yud corresponding to the Ten Commandments. His masoretic note that the phrase 'the abomination of YHWH' (Proverbs 15:8) parallels this spelling ties the golden calf to the category of divine abomination.", :sources ["Exodus 32:19" "Shabbat 87a" "Pesikta Rabbati 23" "Proverbs 15:8"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "The word מידו is written without a second yud (defective spelling), signaling that Israel broke the covenant by denying the Ten Commandments through the golden calf.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וישלך מידו" "תועבת ה'"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וישלך מידו", :refs ["Exodus 32:19"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "תועבת ה'", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :exodus, :voic